[directions] d-15 [open] Compute pure-higgsino thermal relic density Omega h^2 at m_c; d-16 [open] Survey recent arXiv literature on higgsino thermal relic tar; d-17 [open] Place thermal higgsino (1.0-1.2 TeV) relative to LZ 2024 (24; d-18 [open] Quantify thermal higgsino annihilation cross-section <sigma 
**Plan** — 4 lines of investigation:
1. Compute pure-higgsino thermal relic density Omega h^2 at m_chi = 0.9, 1.0, 1.1, 1.15, 1.2, 1.3 TeV with serve-idm tools, interpolate thermal mass where Omega h^2 = 0.120 +/- 0.001 (Planck 2018), and quantify offset from literature Sommerfeld+coannihilation+bound-state values. — Directly answers where the thermal target sits and anchors all limit comparisons. Previous d-09 obtained 1159 GeV perturbatively but flagged missing Sommerfeld/bound-state physics; this direction reproduces the grid, documents tool limitations, and compares to published 1.0-1.2 TeV band.
2. Survey recent arXiv literature on higgsino thermal relic target 1.0-1.2 TeV: canonical 1.1 TeV with Sommerfeld/coannihilation, light-slepton coannihilation lowering to 0.4-0.6 TeV, low-reheating raising mass, and 2026 LZ 248 keV inelastic interpretation (2609.01504, 2609.04175, 2609.33869). — Provides published context for tool results and theoretical uncertainty. Brief lists three 2026 papers that reinterpret thermal mass and direct-detection visibility; no direction has yet extracted their figures/quotes systematically.
3. Place thermal higgsino (1.0-1.2 TeV) relative to LZ 2024 (2410.17036) and XENONnT (2303.14729) SI limits and xenon neutrino fog, distinguishing elastic (suppressed to <1e-48 cm2) vs Z-mediated inelastic (delta threshold ~364 keV on Xe) and mapping (m_chi, delta) allowed region. — Answers 'where does higgsino sit relative to current limits'. Previous d-02/d-05 showed elastic pure higgsino >1.8 decades below LZ at 1.1 TeV but lacked 1 TeV limit reads and fog numbers; d-10 scan found only delta<~365 keV yields events, in tension with 2609.01590 481-519 keV claim.
4. Quantify thermal higgsino annihilation cross-section <sigma v> vs Fermi-LAT dwarf/GC line limits and CTAO-North projected sensitivity — Brief requires <sigma v> vs Fermi-LAT and CTAO as key quantity; d-15/d-17 only record pass/fail flags from check_all_constraints. Dedicated extraction needed to place 1.1 TeV thermal target relative to current line limits and future reach. (added by the critic)
Critic's view: revise — Exceeds 10-call budget: 1x describe_tools + 7x compute_relic_density (900-1300 GeV) + 4-10x check_all_constraints + read_arxiv_chunk/cite/web_search = 13-18 calls. Reduce to 5 masses (1.0,1.1,1.15,1.2,1.3 TeV) and 3 check_all_constraints points.; Notes delta-independence bug f-021 but does not test it. Add explicit check: compute_relic_density at fixed m_chi=1.1 TeV for delta=200 vs 500 keV to document bug, and qualify thermal mass as perturbative only (missing Sommerfeld/bound-state ~10% uncertainty).; Exceeds budget and risks unverifiable claims: web_search for 7 IDs + 2-3x get_paper_figures + multiple read_arxiv_chunk/cite >10 calls. Three 2609.0xxxx papers are dated Sep 2026 and may not resolve via web_search/arXiv HTML; direction has no fallback to established literature (1411.6930, 2205.04486, 1912.07795, 1104.0228) if fetch fails..
