**Blocked — Survey recent arXiv literature on higgsino thermal relic target 1.0-1.2 TeV: canonical 1.1 TeV with Sommerfeld/coannihilation, light-slepton coannihilation lowering to 0.4-0.6 TeV, low-reheating raising mass, and 2026 LZ 248 keV inelastic interpretation (2609.01504, 2609.04175, 2609.33869)..** (Tool budget exhausted after 3 web_search + 3 get_paper_figures; read_arxiv_chunk/read_text_file/cite not executed. Need additional budget to validate verbatim quotes and extract second figure via PDF fallback.) Survey of higgsino thermal relic target partially completed. Established: canonical pure-higgsino thermal mass ~1.1 TeV (band 1.0-1.2 TeV) with Sommerfeld/coannihilation (web_search snippets from 2205.04486, 1912.07795 context) and light-slepton coannihilation lowering to ~0.4-0.6 TeV (Dec 2025 MSSM paper: as light as ~400 GeV) [f-042]. 2026 LZ 248 keV inelastic interpretation: 2609.01504 Higgsino Above Sea of Fog (inelastic DM, nearly degenerate states, high purity near neutrino fog), 2609.04175 TeV higgsino delta~350 keV (specifically 377 keV benchmark) explaining 248 keV event with joint ROI+sideband fit, 2609.33869 low-reheating T_rh<=595 GeV accommodating heavy ~0.1 PeV higgsino while explaining LZ event [f-043]. Extracted 1 figure: arXiv:2609.04175 Figure 1 (fig01.png) at /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-higgsino-dd/runs/261102_180028/figures_2609.04175/fig01.png showing LZ S1c-S2c plane (black ROI, red sideband 800<S1c<1700 phd zero events, gold star 248 keV), F^2(E_R) for natural Xe, and recoil spectra in 2.84 tonne-yr at delta=377 keV (SHM v_esc=544 km/s Helm) predicting 11% ROI / 36% gap / 53% sideband [f-047]. Output dir was empty at start; inelastic-DM server confirmed with Planck Omega h2=0.12+-0.0012 and LZ 248+-23 keV data [f-048]. Remaining open: verbatim thermal-mass quotes with cite() for >=2 papers not yet validated (budget exhausted before read_arxiv_chunk/cite) [x-12]; second figure required but get_paper_figures failed for 2609.01504 and 2609.33869 (no HTML rendering, PDF-only/tikz) [x-11]; need PDF-based figure extraction and systematic quote validation in follow-up run.
