**Critic, wave 1** — continue: 9 findings stand up to the evidence, 5 questioned ('Z-mediated inelastic cross section at 1100 GeV is sigma_n=7.4e-39 cm2 (tool auto for higgs': Evidence shows Z-mediated sigma_n=7.43e-39 cm2 at 1100 GeV (tc-48, tc-51) but does not contain the elastic <1e-48 cm2 value or Chen-Hill 1912.07795 citation. The N~1.1e7 events in tc-51 uses the same 7.4e-39 cm2, not a suppressed cross-section, so the >9 dex suppression inference is not directly evidenced.; 'Canonical pure-higgsino thermal relic mass is ~1.1 TeV (band 1.0-1.2 TeV) with Sommerfeld/': Evidence supports canonical ~1.1 TeV thermal mass (tc-39, tc-52, tc-54) but excerpts are truncated and do not contain the quantitative band 1.0-1.2 TeV or the light-slepton coannihilation numbers ~0.4-0.6 TeV / ~400 GeV claimed.; '2026 LZ 248 keV event interpreted as inelastic higgsino scattering with delta ~300-350 keV': Evidence supports delta~350 keV at ~1.1 TeV (tc-54) and low-reheating 0.1 PeV with T_rh<=595 GeV (tc-38), but does not contain verbatim support for 2609.01504 high-purity/neutrino-fog benchmark or the joint ROI+sideband fit details attributed to 2609.04175.; 'Extracted Figure 1 from arXiv:2609.04175 showing LZ S1c-S2c plane with 248 keV event (gold': Evidence confirms extraction of Figure 1 from 2609.04175 with ROI and sideband boxes (tc-73) but excerpt is truncated before the quantitative predictions 11% ROI / 36% gap / 53% sideband, 2.84 tonne-yr exposure, and delta=377 keV benchmark; those numbers are not in evidence.).

Issues: Thermal mass 1159 GeV is perturbative only (Kolb & Turner, g*=86.25, no Sommerfeld/bound-state/coannihilation). Literature cross-check against 1411.6930 and 2205.04486 to quantify ~10% Sommerfeld uncertainty and ~1-2% perturbative offset not executed; verbatim Planck 0.120+-0.001 quote from 1807.06209 and check_all_constraints at thermal benchmarks missing due to budget.; No numeric LZ 2024 (2410.17036) or XENONnT (2303.14729) SI limits at 1 TeV extracted, no xenon neutrino fog value from XLZD 2410.17137, so 'decades below' and 'below fog' for <1e-48 cm2 elastic prediction remains unquantified. Annual modulation and check_all_constraints benchmarks not run.; Thermal sigma_v ~2.1-3.0e-26 cm3/s established, but no quantitative Fermi-LAT dwarf/GC line 95% CL limits at 1.1 TeV or CTAO-North projected sensitivity numbers extracted; comparison table vs thermal cross-section incomplete, no verbatim quotes or limit figures..
