**Critic, wave 2** — continue: 9 findings stand up to the evidence, 5 questioned ('Web search identifies Fermi-LAT dwarf spheroidal (Ackermann 2015, 1611.03184, 14-yr line s': Evidence excerpts mention dwarf spheroidal galaxies and CTAO-North detection within this decade generically, but do not contain the claimed specific identifiers Ackermann 2015 PRL 115 231301, 1611.03184, 14-yr line search 10 GeV-2 TeV, or any numeric 95% CL values. Quantitative limits not extracted as stated, but specific citations are unsupported by excerpts.; 'Canonical pure-higgsino thermal relic mass is ~1.1 TeV within band 1.0-1.2 TeV including S': Evidence tc-261102_1-w2-d-16-105 only contains phrase 'canonical thermal relic mass of ~1.1 TeV'. It does not contain the claimed band 1.0-1.2 TeV, Sommerfeld/coannihilation correction details, or perturbative value 1.15-1.16 TeV. Second evidence is server description with no mass information.; 'Z-mediated inelastic sigma_n=7.43e-39 cm2 at 1100 GeV vs elastic Higgs-mediated suppressed': Evidence shows tool returns identical sigma_n=7.4299e-39 cm2 for both delta=200 keV and delta=0 keV cases and N=1.1e7 for elastic. It does not contain the claimed elastic suppression to <1e-48 cm2 or Chen-Hill 1912.07795 reference. The >9 dex suppression is an external literature inference not demonstrated by the tool output, which actually uses unsuppressed cross section for elastic.; 'arXiv:2609.01504 Higgsino Above Sea of Fog derives LZ/XENONnT purity bounds on gaugino mix': Evidence tc-261102_1-w2-d-16-97 is a generic web-search snippet about higgsino as inelastic DM and LZ single event; tc-261102_1-w2-d-16-79 is server description. Neither contains purity bounds on gaugino mixing, neutrino fog, or benchmark delta~350 keV claimed for 2609.01504.).

